Subject: [PATCH] shared/ad: return NULL when bt_ad_has_data has no ad

bt_ad_has_data returns struct bt_ad_data *, not bool. Returning false
fails to compile when false has boolean type rather than being an integer
null pointer constant. Return NULL, as for an unsuccessful queue_find.

--- a/src/shared/ad.c
+++ b/src/shared/ad.c
@@ -1247,9 +1247,9 @@
 struct bt_ad_data *bt_ad_has_data(struct bt_ad *ad,
 					const struct bt_ad_data *data)
 {
 	if (!ad)
-		return false;
+		return NULL;

 	return queue_find(ad->data, data_match, data);
 }
